*** HONEST LIMIT — this DB assertion is NON-DISCRIMINATING on store 4116. ***
The commission success path does: $store->store_business_model='commission'; $store->save();
and StoreSubscription::where(store_id)->update(status=0). Store 4116 is ALREADY
'commission', so the Eloquent model is not dirty and save() would emit no UPDATE
(updated_at would not move either); and it has 0 store_subscriptions rows, so the
builder update would affect 0 rows. A successful 200 would therefore have left the
DB byte-identical to a 403. The DB re-read CORROBORATES but CANNOT discriminate.
The discriminating instrument for AC#4 is the HTTP status + body shape above.
No operating store with store_business_model='subscription' exists in multi_food_db
(measured: 0), so no non-vacuous live mutation target is reachable read-only.
